# Backend Documentation

## Overview

The backend is built with Laravel and follows a repository pattern. It's organized into different namespaces for Admin, CustomerWebsite, and CustomerApp.

## Project Structure

```
app/
├── Http/
│   ├── Controllers/
│   │   ├── Admin/
│   │   ├── CustomerWebsite/
│   │   └── CustomerApp/
│   ├── Requests/
│   │   ├── Admin/
│   │   ├── CustomerWebsite/
│   │   └── CustomerApp/
│   └── Resources/
│       ├── Admin/
│       ├── CustomerWebsite/
│       └── CustomerApp/
├── Models/
├── Repositories/
│   ├── Admin/
│   ├── CustomerWebsite/
│   └── CustomerApp/
├── Services/
└── Providers/
```

## Models

{% for model in models %}
- {{ model }}
{% endfor %}

## Repositories

Each model has a corresponding repository in each namespace:

{% for namespace in namespaces %}
### {{ namespace }}
{% for model in models %}
- {{ model }}Repository
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

## Controllers

Controllers are organized by namespace and follow RESTful conventions.

## Form Requests

Form requests are used for validation and are located in the `app/Http/Requests` directory.

## Resources

API Resources are used for transforming models and are located in the `app/Http/Resources` directory.

## Services

Any complex business logic is encapsulated in service classes in the `app/Services` directory.

## Testing

Unit and integration tests are located in the `tests` directory. Run tests using `php artisan test`.

## API Documentation

Refer to the [API Documentation](api.md) for detailed information about available endpoints.